# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Hishab — example environment file
#
# Copy this to `.env` for local development notes. `.env` is git-ignored; this
# example is not.
#
# IMPORTANT: the application does **not** read a `.env` file at runtime.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime configuration (wallets, defaults, the optional online-interpretation
# endpoint and language) lives inside the app, in Settings, and is stored in the
# local SQLite database. The one secret — the online-interpretation bearer
# token — is entered by the user and kept in the platform keystore, never in a
# file and never in the build.
#
# The variables below are for the *build machine / developer shell* only. They
# are consumed by `env.sh` when you `source` it before running Flutter/Dart
# commands. They contain no secrets.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── Local toolchain (this project was built against a locally installed SDK) ──
# Path to the Flutter SDK (`flutter/bin` is added to PATH).
FLUTTER_ROOT=/home/groot/development/flutter

# Home for the Dart package cache.
PUB_CACHE=/home/groot/development/pub-cache

# JDK 17 (required by the Android Gradle Plugin used here).
JAVA_HOME=/home/groot/development/jdk-17

# Android SDK (command-line tools, platform-tools, build-tools).
ANDROID_SDK_ROOT=/home/groot/development/android-sdk
ANDROID_HOME=/home/groot/development/android-sdk


# ── Optional: default online-interpretation endpoint (NON-SECRET) ─────────────
# If you build a custom APK and want the "Online interpretation" endpoint
# pre-filled for your users, you may pass it as a compile-time define:
#
#   flutter build apk --release \
#     --dart-define=PFM_CLOUD_SPEECH_ENDPOINT=https://your-server.example/interpret \
#     --dart-define=PFM_CLOUD_SPEECH_LANGUAGE=bn-BD
#
# Only a NON-SECRET endpoint/language may go here. NEVER put the bearer token in
# a `--dart-define`: everything compiled this way is extractable from the APK.
# Users still paste the token themselves in Settings → Voice entry, and it stays
# in secure storage. Online interpretation remains off until it is explicitly
# enabled in the app.
PFM_CLOUD_SPEECH_ENDPOINT=
PFM_CLOUD_SPEECH_LANGUAGE=bn-BD
